WEBVTT

00:00.100 --> 00:01.300
<b>Yes, it does.</b>

00:01.740 --> 00:08.200
<b>I think he takes the cursed
trading card to a shrine.</b>

00:08.850 --> 00:12.280
<b>That connection wasn't explained
in the episode.</b>

00:12.550 --> 00:16.780
<b>And it was only explained
in the booklet.</b>

00:16.890 --> 00:19.690
<b>Can you explain that part a bit?</b>

00:19.790 --> 00:20.980
<b>What!?</b>

00:34.300 --> 00:35.860
<b>Was it really connected?</b>

00:35.970 --> 00:37.340
<b>Yes, it was.</b>

00:37.440 --> 00:44.080
<b>Note: Kandamyojin is a shrine in the
Kanda district of the Tokyo Prefecture.</b>

00:37.440 --> 00:40.540
<b>It's when he goes
to Kandamyojin, right?</b>

00:40.540 --> 00:42.350
<b>Wasn't that one of the specials?</b>

00:42.350 --> 00:44.080
<b>Was that it?</b>

00:44.550 --> 00:54.820
<b>Note: This occurs in episode 2 of
the Di Gi Charat Summer Special 2000.</b>

00:44.550 --> 00:45.150
<b>Dejiko wanted a reason
for running late.</b>

00:45.150 --> 00:47.780
<b>Dejiko wanted a reason
for running late.</b>

00:47.780 --> 00:48.950
<b>That was it.</b>

00:48.950 --> 00:52.490
<b>But Dejiko lives in Gamers,
so she has no reason to be late.</b>

00:52.490 --> 00:54.820
<b>So they end up
going to Kandamyojin.</b>

00:54.930 --> 00:59.860
<b>And that's how they pull
this old story into it.</b>

00:59.860 --> 01:03.920
<b>So there was no conclusion initially,
but the story continued.</b>

01:04.030 --> 01:09.200
<b>It's probably more like they remembered
the episode and forced a connection.</b>

01:12.080 --> 01:20.310
<b>Note: Shime-nawa is a ''holy rope'' that
is tied around trees and other objects
in the shrine grounds.</b>

01:12.080 --> 01:15.250
<b>I like how the ''shime-nawa'' flies
around in the Di Gi Charat World.</b>

01:16.610 --> 01:20.310
<b>I've seen it often in the anime.</b>

01:20.420 --> 01:25.080
<b>I think so too.
Just as often as the ''kuukan.''</b>

01:29.830 --> 01:31.590
<b>What's this?</b>

01:35.000 --> 01:37.160
<b>I don't get it at all.</b>

01:47.240 --> 01:51.080
<b>Was there a model
for this mountain too?</b>

01:51.180 --> 01:55.710
<b>In the storyboard, it said, ''Scary
mountain with a rope flying in the air.''</b>

01:55.820 --> 01:57.840
<b>And you feel kinda different gema?
Yes gema.</b>

01:57.960 --> 02:00.120
<b>A sudden urge to eat meat.</b>

02:06.060 --> 02:09.830
<b>Was this Usa-copter
an anime original?</b>

02:09.930 --> 02:11.490
<b>Oh, that was me.</b>

02:11.600 --> 02:16.200
<b>It first appeared
in the four-panel manga.</b>

02:17.470 --> 02:20.770
<b>But we didn't expect it
to be used this often,</b>

02:20.880 --> 02:23.180
<b>or become her special ability.</b>

02:31.920 --> 02:33.450
<b>This character's name is really long.</b>

02:33.560 --> 02:35.460
<b>I still can't remember it all.</b>

02:36.230 --> 02:38.820
<b>We call it Henna Ikimono
in English too.</b>

02:38.930 --> 02:42.590
<b>It's actually
''Is it crying or laughing or mad or-''</b>

02:42.700 --> 02:44.630
<b>Oh, then Henna Ikimono is-</b>

02:44.740 --> 02:47.530
<b>A shortened name.</b>

02:50.310 --> 02:56.340
<b>The plushie was popular
at conventions</b>

02:56.450 --> 03:00.010
<b>a couple of years ago.</b>

03:00.680 --> 03:05.520
<b>It was the best selling plushie
in the U.S.</b>

03:05.790 --> 03:09.450
<b>What part of this character
is cute to Americans?</b>

03:09.560 --> 03:11.960
<b>Is it because he's a bear?</b>

03:12.060 --> 03:16.930
<b>I don't know if it's because he's a bear
or because he doesn't make any sense.</b>

03:17.030 --> 03:21.970
<b>There was a Gema plush,
Henna Ikimono plush,</b>

03:22.070 --> 03:24.040
<b>and a Majin Gappa plush
back then.</b>

03:24.140 --> 03:25.400
<b>Yes, there were.</b>

03:25.510 --> 03:30.280
<b>Out of those plushies,
maybe it was the cutest?</b>

03:30.550 --> 03:36.490
<b>Possibly because the plush
came out of the box?</b>

03:36.590 --> 03:39.210
<b>That could be why.</b>

03:43.960 --> 03:46.460
<b>Here's a picture of Gamers.</b>
